<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Williamsburg, Virginia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Williamsburg is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, between the James and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> rivers. It was the capital of the colony of Virginia from 1699 to 1780, when the government moved to Richmond, and is home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/college-of-william-and-mary">College of William &amp; Mary</a>. Its colonial centre, restored from the 1920s as Colonial Williamsburg, is a large living-history museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/williamsburg-virginia.jpg" alt="Williamsburg, Virginia" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ron Cogswell · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Governor%27s_Palace_--_Williamsburg_(VA)_September_2012.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
